# SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

# What Scripts/build-xcframework.sh produces: the archives it passes to
# `xcodebuild -create-xcframework` and the framework itself. Output, and the
# consumer keeps its own copy of the artefact.
build/
*.xcframework

# What /graphify writes: the extracted graph, its report and the interactive
# page. Generated from the sources beside it and regenerated on demand, so it
# is output like `build/` and not part of the package.
graphify-out/

.DS_Store

# Generated by XcodeGen from project.yml, and only so that
# Scripts/build-xcframework.sh has a framework target to archive. The name
# follows `name:` in project.yml, and is worth checking against it: the rule
# here said RMDoc.xcodeproj long enough that RMCloud.xcodeproj was committed
# instead of ignored — the same way RMMarks and RMLines lost the argument
# before it. `.swiftlint.yml` excludes the same directory, and if the two ever
# disagree again, that file is the one telling the truth.
RMCloud.xcodeproj/

# The framework this one links against, and it is committed: it is the
# application's own artefact, the version has to agree with it, and a clone
# has to build with no network. The `*.xcframework` rule above is about what
# this package *produces*, so the one it *consumes* is named back in.
!ThirdParty/**
!ThirdParty/**/*.xcframework
